(1218,2598,'DEF: Inflammation of the conjunctiva, most commonly due to an allergic reaction or an infection. REF: {http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conjunctivitis }','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:14',NULL,NULL,'5869FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1219,2600,'Disorder of cardiac function due to an imbalance between myocardial function and the capacity of the coronary vessels to supply sufficient flow for normal function. It is a form of MYOCARDIAL ISCHEMIA (insufficient blood supply to the heart muscle) caused by a decreased capacity of the coronary vessels.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:14',NULL,NULL,'5840FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1220,2607,'An affective disorder characterized by periods of depression and hypomania. These may be separated by periods of normal mood.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:14',NULL,NULL,'5808FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1221,2608,'General term for cysts and cystic diseases of the ovary.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:14',NULL,NULL,'5805FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1222,2609,'Inflammation of the urinary bladder. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5799FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1223,2611,'An acquired organic mental disorder with loss of intellectual abilities of sufficient severity to interfere with social or occupational functioning. The dysfunction is multifaceted and involves memory, behavior, personality, judgment, attention, spatial relations, language, abstract thought, and other executive functions. The intellectual decline is usually progressive, and initially spares the level of consciousness.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5777FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1224,2614,'A disorder characterized by CONFUSION; inattentiveness; disorientation; ILLUSIONS; HALLUCINATIONS; agitation; and in some instances autonomic nervous system overactivity. It may result from toxic/metabolic conditions or structural brain lesions. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp411-2)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5771FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1225,2615,'A chronic form of schizophrenia characterized primarily by the presence of persecutory or grandiose delusions, often associated with hallucination.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5769FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1226,2616,'Localized destruction of the tooth surface initiated by decalcification of the enamel followed by enzymatic lysis of organic structures and leading to cavity formation. If left unchecked, the cavity may penetrate the enamel and dentin and reach the pulp. The three most prominent theories used to explain the etiology of the disase are that acids produced by bacteria lead to decalcification; that micro-organisms destroy the enamel protein; or that keratolytic micro-organisms produce chelates that lead to decalcification.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5764FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1227,2617,'Disorders related to substance abuse, the side effects of a medication, toxin exposure, and ALCOHOL-RELATED DISORDERS.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5761FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1228,2619,'Lengthy and continuous deprivation of food. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5753FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1229,2620,'Superficial infections of the skin or its appendages by any of various fungi.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'16671FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1230,2621,'Rare, chronic, papulo-vesicular disease characterized by an intensely pruritic eruption consisting of various combinations of symmetrical, erythematous, papular, vesicular, or bullous lesions. The disease is strongly associated with the presence of HLA-B8 and HLA-DR3 antigens. A variety of different autoantibodies has been detected in small numbers in patients with dermatitis herpetiformis.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5747FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1231,2625,'Conditions characterized by language abilities (comprehension and expression of speech and writing) that are below the expected level for a given age, generally in the absence of an intellectual impairment. These conditions may be associated with DEAFNESS; BRAIN DISEASES; MENTAL DISORDERS; or environmental factors.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5734FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1232,2627,'Diabetes characterized by the ability to survive without ketoacidosis in the absence of insulin therapy. It is usually of slow onset and patients exhibit a tendency to obesity.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5720FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1233,2629,'Complication of diabetes resulting from severe insulin deficiency coupled with an absolute or relative increase in glucagon concentration. The metabolic acidosis is caused by the breakdown of adipose stores and resulting increased levels of free fatty acids. Glucagon accelerates the oxidation of the free fatty acids producing excess ketone bodies (ketosis).','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5706FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1234,2630,'Disorders of voice pitch, loudness, or quality. Dysphonia refers to impaired utterance of sounds by the vocal folds.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5697FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1235,2631,'Acute and chronic (see also BRAIN INJURIES, CHRONIC) injuries to the brain, including the cerebral hemispheres, CEREBELLUM, and BRAIN STEM. Clinical manifestations depend on the nature of injury. Diffuse trauma to the brain is frequently associated with DIFFUSE AXONAL INJURY or COMA, POST-TRAUMATIC. Localized injuries may be associated with NEUROBEHAVIORAL MANIFESTATIONS; HEMIPARESIS, or other focal neurologic deficits.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5695FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1236,2632,'A congenital cardiovascular malformation in which the aorta arises entirely from the right ventricle and the pulmonary artery from the left ventricle, so that the venous return from the peripheral circulation is recirculated by the right ventricle via the aorta to the systemic circulation without being oxygenated in the lungs.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5679FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1237,2633,'Infection of humans or animals with hookworms other than those caused by the genus Ancylostoma or Necator, for which the specific terms ANCYLOSTOMIASIS and NECATORIASIS are available.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5662FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1238,2634,'Infections with nematodes of the superfamily FILARIOIDEA. The presence of living worms in the body is mainly asymptomatic but the death of adult worms leads to granulomatous inflammation and permanent fibrosis. Organisms of the genus Elaeophora infect wild elk and domestic sheep causing ischaemic necrosis of the brain, blindness, and dermatosis of the face.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5661FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1239,2636,'ugonjwa wa ubongo','sw',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5641FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1240,2636,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5640FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1241,2639,'DEF: Disease of the cardiovascular system, that is, the heart and blood vessels.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5634FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1242,2642,'Disease of the gastrointestinal tract.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5614FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1243,2645,'A form of bronchial disorder associated with airway obstruction, marked by recurrent attacks of paroxysmal dyspnea, with wheezing due to spasmodic contraction of the bronchi.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5607FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1244,2646,'Variations of menstruation which may be indicative of disease.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5605FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1245,2647,'Diseases of the nail plate and tissues surrounding it. The concept is limited to primates.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5601FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1246,2648,'Diseases of the central and peripheral nervous system. This includes disorders of the brain, spinal cord, cranial nerves, peripheral nerves, nerve roots, autonomic nervous system, neuromuscular junction, and muscle.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1247,2649,'Conditions or disorders affecting the PERITONEUM.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5595FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1248,2657,'Diseases of the urinary tract in both male and female. It does not include the male genitalia for which UROGENITAL DISEASES is used for general discussions of diseases of both the urinary tract and the genitalia.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5558FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1249,2658,'DEF: Disturbance of vision','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5555FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1250,2660,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:15',NULL,NULL,'5541FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1251,2661,'An acute form of TUBERCULOSIS in which minute tubercles are formed in a number of organs of the body due to dissemination of the bacilli through the blood stream.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5535FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1252,2662,'State in which an individual perceives or experiences a sensation of unreality concerning the self or the environment; it is seen in disorders such as schizophrenia, affection disorders, organic mental disorders, and personality disorders. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1253,2664,'Organic mental disorders in which there is impairment of the ability to maintain awareness of self and environment and to respond to environmental stimuli. Dysfunction of the cerebral hemispheres or brain stem RETICULAR FORMATION may result in this condition.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5524FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1254,2665,'Psychotic organic mental disorders resulting from the toxic effect of drugs and chemicals or other harmful substance.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1255,2668,'Difficulty in swallowing.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5495FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1256,2670,'Chronically depressed mood that occurs for most of the day more days than not for at least 2 years. The required minimum duration in children to make this diagnosis is 1 year. During periods of depressed mood, at least 2 of the following additional symptoms are present: poor appetite or overeating, insomnia or hypersomnia, low energy or fatigue, low self esteem, poor concentration or difficulty making decisions, and feelings of hopelessness. (DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5488FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1257,2672,'A group of disorders characterized by physiological and psychological disturbances in appetite or food intake.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5479FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1258,2674,'Onset of convulsions or coma in a previously diagnosed pre-eclamptic patient.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5475FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1259,2676,'Accumulation of watery fluid in the cavity of a joint. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5459FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1260,2677,'The inability to generate oral-verbal expression, despite normal comprehension of speech. This may be associated with BRAIN DISEASES or MENTAL DISORDERS. Organic mutism may be associated with damage to the FRONTAL LOBE; BRAIN STEM; THALAMUS; and CEREBELLUM. Selective mutism is a psychological condition that usually affects children characterized by continuous refusal to speak in social situations by a child who is able and willing to speak to selected persons. Kussmal aphasia refers to mutism in psychosis. (From Fortschr Neurol Psychiatr 1994; 62(9):337-44)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5457FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1261,2678,'Localized destruction of the tooth surface initiated by decalcification of the enamel followed by enzymatic lysis of organic structures and leading to cavity formation. If left unchecked, the cavity may penetrate the enamel and dentin and reach the pulp. The three most prominent theories used to explain the etiology of the disase are that acids produced by bacteria lead to decalcification; that micro-organisms destroy the enamel protein; or that keratolytic micro-organisms produce chelates that lead to decalcification.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1262,2680,'Enlargement of the thyroid gland.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5438FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1263,2681,'A condition in which tissue more or less perfectly resembling the uterine mucous membrane (the endometrium) and containing typical endometrial granular and stromal elements occurs aberrantly in various locations in the pelvic cavity.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5433FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1264,2682,'A condition in which tissue more or less perfectly resembling the uterine mucous membrane (the endometrium) and containing typical endometrial granular and stromal elements occurs aberrantly in various locations in the pelvic cavity.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5432FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1265,2684,'A disorder characterized by recurrent episodes of paroxysmal brain dysfunction due to a sudden, disorderly, and excessive neuronal discharge. Epilepsy classification systems are generally based upon: (1) clinical features of the seizure episodes (e.g., motor seizure), (2) etiology (e.g., post-traumatic), (3) anatomic site of seizure origin (e.g., frontal lobe seizure), (4) tendency to spread to other structures in the brain, and (5) temporal patterns (e.g., nocturnal epilepsy). (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p313)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5403FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1266,2686,'Inflammation, acute or chronic, of the esophagus caused by bacteria, chemicals, or trauma.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5376FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1267,2688,'Reflux of gastric juice and/or duodenal contents (bile acids, pancreatic juice) into the distal esophagus, commonly due to incompetence of the lower esophageal sphincter. Gastric regurgitation is an extension of this process with entry of fluid into the pharynx or mouth.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:16',NULL,NULL,'5367FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
