(1374,2882,'Abnormally infrequent menstruation.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4172FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1375,2888,'Fractures of the femur.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4165FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1376,2891,'diarrheal illness, usually due to infection','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'151FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1377,2895,'Pathologic process consisting of a partial or complete disruption of the layers of a surgical wound.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4093FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1378,2896,'Disorders related or resulting from abuse or mis-use of opioids.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4090FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1379,2898,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1380,2899,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1381,2900,'A progressive, degenerative joint disease, the most common form of arthritis, especially in older persons. The disease is thought to result not from the aging process but from biochemical changes and biomechanical stresses affecting articular cartilage. In the foreign literature it is often called osteoarthrosis deformans.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:20',NULL,NULL,'4067FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1382,2908,'A genus of parasitic nematodes whose organisms are distributed in Central and South America. Characteristics include a smooth cuticle and an enlarged anterior end.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'4027FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1383,2910,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'4020FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1384,2912,'Movements or behaviors associated with sleep, sleep stages, or partial arousals from sleep that may impair sleep maintenance. Parasomnias are generally divided into four groups: arousal disorders, sleep-wake transition disorders, parasomnias of REM sleep, and nonspecific parasomnias. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p191)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'3998FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1385,2913,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or \"seizure disorder.\"','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'3987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1386,2914,'Fractures occurring as a result of disease of a bone or from some undiscoverable cause, and not due to trauma. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'3985FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1387,2918,'Abnormal enlargement or overgrowth of the gingivae brought about by enlargement of existing cells.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'3968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1388,2921,'Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the circulation and function of tissue within that space. Compartmentation involves mainly the leg but also involved are the forearm, arm, thigh, shoulder, and buttock. Some of the causes of increased pressure are trauma, tight dressings, hemorrhage, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression, paralysis, and contracture.','en',2,'2026-06-24 10:48:21',NULL,NULL,'3959FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
